</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Housley</surname><given-names>M. P.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Hart</surname><given-names>G. W.</given-names></name> <article-title>O-GlcNAc cycling: How a single sugar post-translational modification is changing the way we think about signaling networks</article-title>. <source>J. Cell. Biochem.</source> <year>2006</year>, <volume>97</volume>, 71&#x02013;83.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16237703</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref7"><citation id="cit7" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Haines</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Irvine</surname><given-names>K. D.</given-names></name> <article-title>Glycosylation regulates Notch signalling</article-title>. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <year>2003</year>, <volume>4</volume>, 786&#x02013;797.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14570055</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref8"><citation id="cit8" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Herrmann</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>von der Lieth</surname><given-names>C. W.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Stehling</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Reutter</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Pawlita</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name> <article-title>Consequences of a subtle sialic acid modification on the murine polyomavirus receptor</article-title>. <source>J. Virol.</source> <year>1997</year>, <volume>71</volume>, 5922&#x02013;5931.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9223482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref9"><citation id="cit9" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name> <article-title>Sialobiology of influenza: Molecular mechanism of host range variation of influenza viruses</article-title>. <source>Biol. Pharm. Bull.</source> <year>2005</year>, <volume>28</volume>, 399&#x02013;408.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15744059</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><citation id="cit10" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Upreti</surname><given-names>R. K.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Shankar</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name> <article-title>Bacterial glycoproteins: Functions, biosynthesis and applications</article-title>. <source>Proteomics</source> <year>2003</year>, <volume>3</volume>, 363&#x02013;379.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12687605</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><citation id="cit11" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Dube</surname><given-names>D. H.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Bertozzi</surname><given-names>C. R.</given-names></name> <article-title>Glycans in cancer and inflammation--potential for therapeutics and diagnostics</article-title>. <source>Nat. Rev. Drug Discovery</source> <year>2005</year>, <volume>4</volume>, 477&#x02013;488.</citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><citation id="cit12" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Lowe</surname><given-names>J. B.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Marth</surname><given-names>J. D.</given-names></name> <article-title>A genetic approach to mammalian glycan function</article-title>. <source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source> <year>2003</year>, <volume>72</volume>, 643&#x02013;691.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676797</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><citation id="cit13" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Stanley</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Ioffe</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name> <article-title>Glycosyltransferase mutants: Key to new insights in glycobiology</article-title>. <source>FASEB J.</source> <year>1995</year>, <volume>9</volume>, 1436&#x02013;1444.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7589985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><citation id="cit14" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Feizi</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Fazio</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Chai</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>C. H.</given-names></name> <article-title>Carbohydrate microarrays - a new set of technologies at the frontiers of glycomics</article-title>. <source>Curr. Opin. Struct. Biol.</source> <year>2003</year>, <volume>13</volume>, 637&#x02013;645.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14568620</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><citation id="cit15" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Ostash</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name> <article-title>Bacterial transglycosylase inhibitors</article-title>. <source>Curr. Opin. Chem. Biol.</source> <year>2005</year>, <volume>9</volume>, 459&#x02013;466.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16118062</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><citation id="cit16" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Fuster</surname><given-names>M. M.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Esko</surname><given-names>J. D.</given-names></name> <article-title>The sweet and sour of cancer: Glycans as novel therapeutic targets</article-title>. <source>Nat. Rev. Cancer</source> <year>2005</year>, <volume>5</volume>, 526&#x02013;542.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16069816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><citation id="cit17" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Lairson</surname><given-names>L. L.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Withers</surname><given-names>S. G.</given-names></name> <article-title>Mechanistic analogies amongst carbohydrate modifying enzymes</article-title>. <source>Chem. Commun.</source> <year>2004</year>, 2243&#x02013;2248.</citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><citation id="cit18" citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Kiessling</surname><given-names>L. L.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Gestwicki</surname><given-names>J. E.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Strong</surname><given-names>L. E.</given-names></name> <article-title>Syntheti